    "termsOfUse": "The data can be accessed and reused by researchers affiliated with universities or no-profit, non-commercial organizations specifically associated to one or more of the following categories:\n\n1. Researchers working in the following disciplinary fields\n- Audience studies (art, media, film)\n- Film studies\n- Media studies\n- Media psychology\n- Contemplative science\n- Mindfulness studies\n- Arts sociology\n- Critical theory\n\n2. Researchers with expertise in the study of consciousness from various theoretical and\nmethodological frameworks, including:\n- Phenomenolog\n- (Cognitive) Neuroscience\n- Psychology\n- Ethnography\n\n3. Researchers with an expertise in the following topics:\n- Slowness\n- Attention\n- Time perception\n- Art experience",
    "restrictions": "The data is not privacy sensitive. However, as participants did not have an opportunity to express their thoughts on data reuse, a customized license applies, ensuring that reuse of data adheres to ethical standards and the scientific code of conduct (https://doi.org/10.17026/dans-2cj-nvwu, 2018). ",
